WEBVTT

00:00:16.192 --> 00:00:17.846
Harry?

00:00:17.846 --> 00:00:20.457
Professor, sir.

00:00:20.457 --> 00:00:22.459
Your bird--

00:00:22.459 --> 00:00:24.635
There was nothing I could do.

00:00:24.635 --> 00:00:26.376
He just caught fire.

00:00:26.376 --> 00:00:28.335
Oh, and about time too.

00:00:28.335 --> 00:00:31.686
He's been looking
dreadful for days.

00:00:31.686 --> 00:00:33.644
Pity you had to see him
on a burning day.

00:00:36.734 --> 00:00:39.172
Fawkes is a phoenix, Harry.

00:00:39.172 --> 00:00:42.740
They burst into flame
when it is time for them to die,

00:00:42.740 --> 00:00:46.657
and then they are...
reborn from the ashes.

00:00:56.102 --> 00:00:58.931
Fascinating creatures,
phoenixes.

00:00:58.931 --> 00:01:02.847
They can carry immensely
heavy loads,

00:01:02.847 --> 00:01:06.242
and their tears
have healing powers.

00:01:06.242 --> 00:01:08.244
[DOOR OPENS]

00:01:08.244 --> 00:01:11.247
Professor Dumbledore, sir.
Wait, listen.

00:01:12.683 --> 00:01:14.424
Professor Dumbledore, sir.
It wasn't Harry.

00:01:14.424 --> 00:01:16.035
Ah, Hagrid...

00:01:16.035 --> 00:01:18.037
I'd swear it in front
of the Ministry of Magic.

00:01:18.037 --> 00:01:20.082
Hagrid!

00:01:20.082 --> 00:01:23.346
Relax.

00:01:23.346 --> 00:01:27.524
I do not believe
that Harry attacked anyone.

00:01:27.524 --> 00:01:29.657
Of course you don't.
And--

00:01:29.657 --> 00:01:33.269
Oh. Oh...

00:01:33.269 --> 00:01:36.490
Right. Well, I'll--
I'll just wait outside, then.

00:01:36.490 --> 00:01:38.405
Yes.

00:01:41.843 --> 00:01:43.932
You don't think it was me,
professor?

00:01:43.932 --> 00:01:47.631
No, Harry.
I do not think it was you.

00:01:49.720 --> 00:01:51.287
But I must ask you...

00:01:51.287 --> 00:01:55.944
is there something
you wish to tell me?

00:02:02.211 --> 00:02:03.734
No, sir.

00:02:03.734 --> 00:02:05.519
Nothing.

00:02:08.870 --> 00:02:10.263
Very well, then.

00:02:10.263 --> 00:02:12.004
Off you go.

00:02:18.706 --> 00:02:21.056
[♪♪♪]

00:02:50.694 --> 00:02:52.305
Everything's set.

00:02:52.305 --> 00:02:54.220
We just need a bit of who
you're changing into.

00:02:54.220 --> 00:02:55.656
Crabbe and Goyle.

00:02:55.656 --> 00:02:57.962
We also need
to make sure

00:02:57.962 --> 00:03:00.617
that the real Crabbe and Goyle
can't burst in on us

00:03:00.617 --> 00:03:02.880
while
we're interrogating Malfoy.

00:03:02.880 --> 00:03:04.404
How?

00:03:04.404 --> 00:03:06.319
I've got it all worked out.

00:03:06.319 --> 00:03:09.278
I filled these
with a simple sleeping draught.

00:03:09.278 --> 00:03:11.628
Simple, but powerful.

00:03:11.628 --> 00:03:14.283
Now, once they're asleep,

00:03:14.283 --> 00:03:15.937
hide them
in the broomstick cupboard,

00:03:15.937 --> 00:03:17.678
and pull out
a few of their hairs,

00:03:17.678 --> 00:03:19.332
and put on
their uniforms.

00:03:19.332 --> 00:03:20.855
Whose hair are you
ripping out, then?

00:03:20.855 --> 00:03:23.205
I've already got mine.

00:03:23.205 --> 00:03:26.165
Millicent Bulstrode.
Slytherin.

00:03:26.165 --> 00:03:27.992
I got this off her robes.

00:03:27.992 --> 00:03:31.300
I'm going to go check
on the Polyjuice Potion.

00:03:31.300 --> 00:03:34.086
Make sure that Crabbe and Goyle
find these.

00:03:44.270 --> 00:03:46.576
Ahem.

00:03:46.576 --> 00:03:49.057
Ron, maybe
I should do it.

00:03:49.057 --> 00:03:52.887
Yeah. Right.

00:03:52.887 --> 00:03:54.889
Wingardium Leviosa.

00:03:58.414 --> 00:04:00.329
[DOOR OPENING]

00:04:04.681 --> 00:04:05.682
Cool.

00:04:29.532 --> 00:04:31.404
How thick could you get?

00:04:31.404 --> 00:04:33.057
Come on,
let's get them.

00:04:36.104 --> 00:04:37.497
We'll have exactly one hour

00:04:37.497 --> 00:04:39.542
before we change back
into ourselves.

00:04:48.203 --> 00:04:50.466
Add the hairs.

00:04:53.295 --> 00:04:56.168
Ew. Essence of Crabbe.

00:04:56.168 --> 00:04:57.473
Cheers.

00:05:07.353 --> 00:05:08.658
I think I'm gonna be sick.

00:05:12.836 --> 00:05:15.622
Me too.

